r\n\r\n```diff\r\n-Index(\"ix_unique\", \"foo\", unique=True)\r\n+Index(\"ix_unique\", \"foo\", \"bar\", unique=True)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe downgrade generates a non-unique index.\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\n\r\nThe downgrade should preserve the `unique` flag.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nPlease try to provide a [Minimal, Complete, and Verifiable](http://stackoverflow.com/help/mcve) example, with the migration script and/or the SQLAlchemy tables or models involved.\r\nSee also [Reporting Bugs](https://www.sqlalchemy.org/participate.html#bugs) on the website.\r\n\r\n```py\r\nfrom alembic.operations import ops\r\n\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, Index, Integer, MetaData, Table\r\n\r\nmetadata = MetaData()\r\ntable = Table(\r\n    \"t\",\r\n    metadata,\r\n    Column(\"id\", Integer(), primary_key=True),\r\n    Column(\"x\", Integer()),\r\n)\r\nix = Index(\"ix1\", table.c.id, unique=True)\r\n\r\nop = ops.CreateIndexOp.from_index(ix)\r\nassert op.reverse().to_index().unique\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Error**\r\n\r\nAssertionError on last line.\r\n\r\n**Versions.**\r\n - OS: Ubuntu\r\n - Python: 3.11\r\n - Alembic: main\r\n - SQLAlchemy: 2.0\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n<!-- Add any other context about the problem here. -->\r\n\r\n**Have a nice day!**\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs",